<title>JAPAN: LTCB bid-only on news of global alliance.</title>
<headline>LTCB bid-only on news of global alliance.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-07-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of the Long-Term Credit Bank of Japan (LTCB) were bid-only on Wednesday morning, cheered by news late on Tuesday that it and Swiss Bank Corp had signed a letter of intent to form a global strategic alliance, traders said.</p>
<p>At 0006 GMT, LTCB shares were bid-only at 432 yen, against Tuesday's close of 427 yen.  </p>
<p>The pillars of the alliance would be joint ventures based in Japan covering investment banking, asset management and private banking, the two banks said on Tuesday.</p>
